text.en:
Pursuant to section 3(3), the Brunei Darussalam fishery limits shall be —

(a) an outer-limit consisting of a line 200 miles distant from the baseline from which the breadth of the territorial sea of Brunei Darussalam is measured;

(b) a lateral boundary with the adjoining territory of Sabah, consisting of the same boundary as was promulgated for the continental shelf of North Borneo by Order-in-Council of 11th September 1958 (S. 1 1958 No. 1517) but continued out to the 200-mile limit by a straight line;

(c) a lateral boundary with the adjoining territory of Sarawak, consisting of the same boundary as was promulgated for the continental shelf of Sarawak by Order-in-Council of 11th September 1958 (S. 1 1958 No. 1518) but continued out to the 200-mile limit by a straight line. Large scale map.
